    "done_when": "This session runs inside the fleet SLURM allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID is set), so run the gate in place, not through srun: TMPDIR=/tmp UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 8 tests/data/test_jt60sa_machine_map.py tests/data/test_description_reader.py tests/data/test_transform_engine.py tests/data/test_description_identity.py tests/data/test_geometry_transitions.py > <your log> 2>&1; echo EXIT=$?. It exits 0 with tests in the new file tests/data/test_jt60sa_machine_map.py asserting: (1) load_packaged_machine_map('jt-60sa') loads imas_ambix/data/machine_maps/jt-60sa.json, which declares description_store_format netcdf, description_store_root JT60SA_DESCRIPTION_DIR (already in imas_ambix/data/paths.py), description_store_layout static-over-map and probe_angle_source description, and exactly two maps with machine jt-60sa: OP1 with first_shot 100001 and last_shot 101173, and OP2 with first_shot 101174 and last_shot 999999; map_for_shot on that catalogue raises LookupError for 60033 and for 1000000. (2) The pf_active coils are declared as MAST's are: one binding family and one structure assembly per coil, each coil-element binding carrying struct_array_entry set to the coil's name as the store carries it, and a source_rank that counts only the leaf and the struct levels below the selected coil. Any other ragged struct array in the five IDS is declared the same way. (3) Against the real store under /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description, read-only: transform_machine_description selects OP1 for 101173 and OP2 for 101174 through one code path; read_geometry_table and geometry_table_from_description build a GeometryTable for each with no comparison against a machine name added to any module; both phases carry the 12 PF coils with 268 coil elements in all (40 x4, 16 x6, 6 x2); the OP1 passive structure carries 120 vessel filaments and the OP2 one 98. (4) The three identity assertions, using machine_description_bytes from imas_ambix/data/description_identity.py as the MAST tests in tests/data/test_description_identity.py do: determinism (two emissions for 101173 are byte-equal), partition consistency (100001 and 101173 emit byte-equal descriptions, and so do 101174 and 150000), and a visible change at the boundary (101173 and 101174 differ, pf_passive is among the differing IDS, pf_active and magnetics are byte-equal across it, and the test prints every differing IDS and field). The existing tests in the other four files still pass; the gate log header names the base revision and the delta against it. UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0. mast.json and diii-d.json are not modified. This node never contacts the JT-60SA server (no ssh jt-60sa, no EDDB call) and never writes under /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa. If geometry_table_from_description or the transform engine needs a change to read the JT-60SA description, stop with status blocked and name the function and the failing field rather than editing either.",
